-New evaluation preserves the nominal decoder first. With no substantial native channel product, it surveys 24 small IQ windows distributed across the entire recording over ±60000 Hz, ranking broad LRPT-like power while clipping narrow interferers. It runs at most two additional full-IQ decodes, using `--freq_shift` before resampling/filtering, without creating another large IQ file. The [base demodulator](https://github.com/SatDump/SatDump/blob/1.2.2/src-core/modules/demod/module_demod_base.cpp) and [rotator](https://github.com/SatDump/SatDump/blob/1.2.2/src-core/common/dsp/utils/freq_shift.cpp) establish the ordering and sign: a candidate carrier at +45000 Hz gets shift -45000 Hz. Metadata distinguishes carrier offset from applied shift. At 256 kS/s, Nyquist is ±128 kHz; an approximately 108 kHz LRPT band displaced by 60 kHz still fits theoretically inside the saved bandwidth. Capture clipping/interference cannot be repaired afterward.
